class Solution {
    public Node removeLastNode(Node head) {
        if (head == null || head.next == null) return null;  // empty or single node → return null

        Node curr = head;                                    // curr starts at head
        Node prev = curr;                                    // prev starts at head (unused)

        while (curr.next.next != null) {                     // stop at second-last node
            curr = curr.next;                                // move curr forward
        }

        curr.next = null;                                    // cut link to last node

        return head;                                         // return updated list
    }
}

//////////////////////// DRY RUN /////////////////////////////

**Dry Run:**

**Input:** `1 -> 2 -> 3 -> null`
```
        Initial:

                head
                 ↓
                [1] -> [2] -> [3] -> null
                 ↑
                curr


        Step 1:

                curr.next.next = [3].next = null → loop ends

                [1] -> [2] -> [3] -> null
                        ↑
                       curr


        Operation:

                curr.next = null

        Final:

                head
                 ↓
                [1] -> [2] -> null
```

✅ Node `3` deleted

---

**Edge Case 1:** `1 -> null`
```
        head.next == null → return null

        Final: null
```

✅ Single node → list becomes empty

---

**Edge Case 2:** `null`
```
        head == null → return null

        Final: null

